# SABOTAGE: T76 (spec §I3 CRM reporting) — defeats the HONEST-EMPTY floor on
# `Samen.Web.CRM.Reads.pipeline_rates/2`. `rate/2`'s zero-denominator clause returns `nil`
# (an org with no closed deals has no win_rate; an org with no opportunities has no
# conversion_rate) — the caller renders `nil` as "—", never a number. This patch swaps the
# zero-denominator clause to `0.0`, fabricating "0% win rate" / "0% conversion" for an org
# that has decided NO deals yet (or created none at all) — the exact "no data → honest
# zero/empty rendering, never fabricated demo numbers" lie the T76 task guards against. A
# tenant reading a fresh org's dashboard would see "Win rate: 0.0%" (reading as "we lose
# every deal") instead of the honest "—" (reading as "no deals decided yet"). Single-org
# fixtures with real closed deals stay green (division proceeds identically either way) —
# only the zero-denominator edge, which the named tests target directly, flips. Reverts
# byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_reporting_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: HONEST EMPTY: an org with NO opportunities gets nil for both rates (never a fabricated 0%)
# MUST_FAIL: HONEST EMPTY (partial): an org with OPEN deals but ZERO closed deals gets nil win_rate but a real (zero) conversion_rate
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
@@ -745,7 +745,7 @@
     _ -> %{win_rate: nil, conversion_rate: nil, won: 0, lost: 0, open: 0, on_hold: 0}
   end

-  defp rate(_won, 0), do: nil
+  defp rate(_won, 0), do: 0.0
   defp rate(won, total), do: won / total

   defp round_count(n) when is_integer(n), do: n
